  "text9": {
   "type": "text",
   "layout": {
    "width": {
     "fill": 0
    },
    "height": {
     "hug": 0
    }
   },
   "props": {
    "style": {
     "from": "lead"
    },
    "text": "Two years ago every one of our services spoke to its neighbours in its own way: HTTP callbacks here, a cron job polling a table there, three different brokers in between. This is the story of folding all of it into a single queue, and what it cost us."
   }
  },
  "text10": {
   "type": "text",
   "layout": {
    "width": {
     "fill": 0
    },
    "height": {
     "hug": 0
    }
   },
   "props": {
    "style": {
     "from": "heading2"
    },
    "text": "Why one queue"
   }
  },
  "Paragraph1": {
   "type": "Paragraph",
   "layout": {
    "width": {
     "fill": 0
    },
    "height": {
     "hug": 0
    }
   },
   "props": {
    "text": "Each integration had been a sensible choice on the day it was made. Together they meant forty failure modes, forty retry policies and no single place to see where a message was stuck. On-call engineers spent more time tracing hops than fixing causes."
   }
  },
  "Paragraph2": {
   "type": "Paragraph",
   "layout": {
    "width": {
     "fill": 0
    },
    "height": {
     "hug": 0
    }
   },
   "props": {
    "text": "We set ourselves a narrow goal: every asynchronous message between services would pass through one durable, partitioned queue with one retry policy and one dashboard."
   }
  },
  "column10": {
   "type": "column",
   "layout": {
    "padding": [
     20,
     12,
     12,
     12
    ],
    "width": {
     "fill": 0
    },
    "height": {
     "hug": 0
    }
   },
   "props": {
    "crossAxisAlignment": "start"
   },
   "decoration": {
